;; KIR4 (agent KIR4, 2026-10-03): the KIR :document. A document is a :string holding its CANONICAL EDN text, the
;; representation stage-0's own native backend uses (kotoba-lang/kotoba-native src/kotoba/native/document.cljk: "the
;; native document IS its canonical EDN text"; no loader operation, no new SIR op, no new ABI). The operations are a
;; second KIR library (the defns of seed/tests/kir/doclib/doclib.kotoba, ports of stage-0's kotoba$doc-* helpers),
;; emitted as ONE group (use bit 8) when a program uses any of them:
;;   :document (a type keyword anywhere: params, result, [:option :document], ..)   -> :string
;;   (document-OP a ..)                    -> (__kr_d.. a ..)   null bool i64 string symbol count kind equal?
;;                                            set-contains? contains get vector-at list-at map-entry-at vector-assoc
;;                                            vector-conj vector-drop vector-remove vector-sort assoc dissoc merge (2 args)
;;                                            string-value bool-value i64-value edn-print edn-read (the last two: identity,
;;                                            as stage-0: a native document is already its EDN text)
;;   (document-keyword :k)                 -> the string literal ":k" (kr-dkw); a non-literal operand stays and 21-check
;;                                            refuses document-keyword by name (a seed keyword has no text at run time)
;;   (document-vector a b ..)              -> (__kr_dbounded (__kr_dvadd (__kr_dvadd (__kr_dvz) a) b) ..)   (kr-dfold)
;;   (document-list ..) / (document-set ..) / (document-map k v ..)   the same fold from () / #{} / {} with __kr_dvadd /
;;                                            __kr_dsetput / __kr_dmapputu (sorted, unique keys, bounded as stage-0)
;; Not supported (left for 21-check to refuse by name): document-keyword-value / document-symbol-value (no keyword or
;; symbol from text in the seed), document-f64*, document-sha256, document-print/read (stage-0 refuses them too).
